USCSandbox: keep the swizzle of a constant-buffer read that takes all components.

A float4 read with four components was always printed without a swizzle, as if it were .xyzw.
The fog distance in a vertex shader, mad(r1.xxxx, cb3[1].zzzz, cb3[1].wwww) in the DXBC, came out as
'tmp1.xxxx * unity_FogParams + unity_FogParams' (seen in the game's PIDI World Based Fog shader).
The mask is now hidden only when it is .xyzw in order.

Licence: GPL-3.0, like USCSandbox (https://github.com/nesrak1/USCSandbox).

diff --git a/USCSandbox/UltraShaderConverter/USIL/Metadders/USILCBufferMetadder.cs b/USCSandbox/UltraShaderConverter/USIL/Metadders/USILCBufferMetadder.cs
index 4123eb1..c33553e 100644
--- a/USCSandbox/UltraShaderConverter/USIL/Metadders/USILCBufferMetadder.cs
+++ b/USCSandbox/UltraShaderConverter/USIL/Metadders/USILCBufferMetadder.cs
@@ -170,7 +170,9 @@ namespace AssetRipper.Export.Modules.Shaders.UltraShaderConverter.USIL.Metadders
                     operand.metadataNameAssigned = true;
                     operand.metadataNameWithArray = param.ArraySize > 1;
 
-                    if (cbMasks.Count == maxRowOrColumnLength && !param.IsMatrix)
+                    // hide the mask only when it is the whole variable in order (.xyzw), not .zzzz or .wwww
+                    if (cbMasks.Count == maxRowOrColumnLength && !param.IsMatrix
+                        && cbMasks.Select((m, i) => m == i).All(x => x))
                     {
                         operand.displayMask = false;
                     }
